# Release Sentinel (Wave 8)

> A single old failure, a fresh cluster, and a live streak are three different
> release stories. This fixture keeps the Wave 8 temporal contrasts explicit and
> anchors the `since the last` check on an event-backed adjective so an
> anchorless history surfaces as `unknown` rather than being flattened.

## Contract (( role: reference ))
- Input: a service.
- Output: a release-health verdict preserving historical, recent, streak, and
  anchorless-since distinctions.

## Workflow — steps

if the deploy step has ever failed,
  Post: "release sentinel saw a prior deploy failure".
if the deploy step has failed within the last 7 days,
  Post: "release sentinel saw a recent deploy failure".
if the deploy step has failed at least 2 times within the last 7 days,
  Post: "release sentinel saw repeated recent deploy failures".
if the deploy step has failed 2 times in a row,
  Post: "release sentinel saw an active deploy failure streak".
if across all runs, the deploy step has ever failed,
  Post: "release sentinel saw a cross-run deploy failure".

## Workflow — steps 2

if the service is recovered since the last deploy step succeeded,
  Post: "release sentinel is healthy since the last successful deploy".
if it is unknown whether:
  Post: "release sentinel has no successful deploy anchor yet".
otherwise,
  Post: "release sentinel is not healthy since the last successful deploy".

## Workflow — steps 3

Post: "release sentinel wave8 pass complete".

## Report shape (( role: template ))
The receipt distinguishes historical failure, recent-window failure, repeated
recent failure, a live failure streak, and since-the-last health with an
explicit unknown/default policy when there is no successful anchor.
